arded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper.\n\nWe need to compare these with B and C. The panel hasn't discussed A and D yet. We need to bring them in. We should argue which candidate is best overall. Let's weigh.\n\nC: strong operational strengths but attitude concerns (show-off, not open to new ideas). No crew cooperation evidence.\n\nB: strong reliability, stress, technical, but can be grumpy and uncooperative, no concrete crew cooperation evidence.\n\nA: quick correct decisions, calm, technical, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Likely poor crew cooperation.\n\nD: problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but hot temper, know-it-all (cooperation), may affect stress resilience.\n\nWhich is best? All have concerns. Perhaps Candidate B still best because reliability and stress resilience are core, and interpersonal issues may be mitigated with training. But we have no concrete evidence of crew cooperation for B either. C has leadership but attitude issues. A has communication issues. D has hot temper.\n\nGiven the safety-critical nature, crew cooperation is essential. B's \"can be uncooperative\" is a red flag. C's \"show-off\" also red flag. A's \"difficulty communicating ideas\" and egocentric also red flag. D's hot temper also red flag.\n\nWe need to pick the candidate with the least severe crew cooperation concerns. Which is less severe? \"Can be uncooperative\" vs \"show-off\" vs \"difficulty communicating\" vs \"hot temper\". Hard to rank. Perhaps \"can be uncooperative\" suggests occasional, while \"hot temper\" could be dangerous under stress. \"Show-off\" may affect teamwork but maybe less dangerous than hot temper. \"Difficulty communicating ideas\" could be serious for cockpit communication.\n\nThus maybe Candidate C still best despite attitude, because leadership and anticipation are critical for long-distance flights. The concerns about being a show-off and not open to new ideas could be mitigated with team culture. So I might stick with Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's suggestion to discuss A and D, and provide some analysis, but still state recommendation. So we can say: I still recommend C, because its operational strengths outweigh the attitude concerns, and the other candidates have more severe crew cooperation or stress issues.\n\nThus vote remains Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: mention that while A and D have issues, C's strengths in anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership are crucial, and the attitude concerns, while noted, are less likely to impair safety than the communication or temper issues of A and D. So I keep recommendation for C.\n\nNow METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C."}
